nt="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="If8e3e7763ce3588fc8f19f0e6d5e02f28d48c1ef" commit="454ab067308cd247dc1d51d07310d39fc91bf237" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ecryptfs: don't allow mmap when the lower fs doesn't support it  There are legitimate reasons to disallow mmap on certain files, notably in sysfs or procfs.  We shouldn't emulate mmap support on file systems that don't offer support natively.  CVE-2016-1583  Signed-off-by: Jeff Mahoney &lt;jeffm@suse.com&gt; Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org [tyhicks: clean up f_op check by using ecryptfs_file_to_lower()] Signed-off-by: Tyler Hicks &lt;tyhicks@canonical.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit f0fe970df3838c202ef6c07a4c2b36838ef0a88b)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55232, chrome-os-partner:55277 TEST=test logins, Files app, etc. still work without ecryptfs errors  Change-Id: If8e3e7763ce3588fc8f19f0e6d5e02f28d48c1ef Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362931 Reviewed-by: Ricky Zhou &lt;rickyz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="362931" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/31/362931/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia92f2925b59839a1f3d66b50ed0ee4d4d59601b7" commit="924380ba4712a5b6b993469636000cfbbb3e2d6a" commit_message="platform_FilePerms: add more android container mount info  Previously, no images were mounted on these directries until ARC is actually started. With CL:*269225 which was submitted recently, squashfs images are mounted with noexec right after Chrome OS boot without waiting for the start-arc-instance Upstart signal.  BUG=chromium:631080 BUG=b:25598471 TEST=platform_FilePerms on cyan-cheets  Change-Id: Ia92f2925b59839a1f3d66b50ed0ee4d4d59601b7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362877 Commit-Ready: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Norvez &lt;norvez@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="362877" owner_email="yusukes@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/77/362877/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2e9c116bc1e0b07d37b540266fd252aee4fd6e84" commit="1bab50daf061127b7eb1d798256a2dc564e44aaf" commit_message="dev: add initial APIs to devserver to support cros auto-update.  This CL adds three APIs on devserver: 1. 'cros_au' API: to support 'start cros auto-update'. 2. 'get_au_status' API: to check the status of cros auto-update. 3. 'collect_au_log' API: to collect auto-update log from devserver. 4. 'handler_cleanup' API: delete the status file for tracking the progress of    CrOS auto-update. 5. 'kill_au_proc' API: to kill unexpected auto-update process for DUT.  Also it updates the unittests and integration test.  The 'cros_au' API triggers a background process to support the whole auto-update processes for a CrOS host, includes: 1. Transfer devserver/stateful update package. 2. If devserver cannot run on the host, restore the stateful partition. 3. If restore_stateful_partiton is not required, and stateful_update is required, do stateful_update. 4. If stateful_update fails, or rootfs_update is required, do rootfs update. 5. Final check after the whole auto-update process.  BUG=chromium:613765 TEST=Locally ran 'ds.auto_update([dut], [image_path])'; Ran 'repair' for dut from local autotest instance; Ran unittest, devserver_integration_test.   Changes to be committed:  modified:   Makefile  new file:   cros_update.py  new file:   cros_update_logging.py  new file:   cros_update_progress.py  new file:   cros_update_unittest.py  modified:   devserver.py  modified:   devserver_integration_test.py  Change-Id: I2e9c116bc1e0b07d37b540266fd252aee4fd6e84 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346199 Commit-Ready: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346199" owner_email="xixuan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/platform/dev-util" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/dev-util" ref="refs/changes/99/346199/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I632537501c0dca4e8693d09b11d0674dcabb8df8" commit="8418c9fa2ba52f9aed0c85b46c13f283c0a0120d" commit_message="adb_host: Sync the UTC time for M and later devices.  The &quot;-u&quot; option in the &quot;date&quot; command sets the UTC time instead of localtime used by the adb host. This patch synchronizes the time of the adb host in the UTC timezone with the autotest server time in the UTC timezone so they match. The previous code was syncing the localtime ignoring the timezones.  BUG=b:30265445 TEST=syntax check; manually test a &quot;date -u&quot; command.  Change-Id: I632537501c0dca4e8693d09b11d0674dcabb8df8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362071 Commit-Ready: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bindu Mahadev &lt;bmahadev@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bryan Lewandowski &lt;bryanlew@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="362071" owner_email="deymo@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/71/362071/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I705817a7246a7a87714ee7352ab748c195b29792" commit="3411b14c02e779c5400dbe56cc610a5a28130e81" commit_message="Cave: Enable software gain on internal microphone and set Mic Volume to 24dB  Enable software gain because there is no capture control for internal microphone. Set maximum software gain to 2000. The default value of &quot;Mic Volume&quot; control is 0dB which is too low. Set the gain to +24dB. This patch also binds the &quot;Mic Volume&quot; control to the sklnau8825max Headset Jack.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54893 BRANCH=master TEST=test pass using alsamixer  Change-Id: I705817a7246a7a87714ee7352ab748c195b29792 Signed-off-by: Shasha Zhao &lt;Sarah_Zhao@asus.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/360637 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="360637" owner_email="Sarah_Zhao@asus.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/37/360637/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie9f8b603a724358946d6265014a90830fdd90837" commit="d676de63c1c0943c2fb6d9ac3a0df42e0116c035" commit_message="Remove bitmap_in_cbfs  This switch is on by default and cannot be turned off, thus it has no effect.  BUG=chromium:622501 BRANCH=none TEST=none  Change-Id: Ie9f8b603a724358946d6265014a90830fdd90837 Signed-off-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362977 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="362977" owner_email="dnojiri@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/77/362977/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ida50458504b501dbd7f630fd65111e920dc5a427" commit="8621f407060ed72266716421edd9ebf0957c7027" commit_message="Remove bitmap_in_cbfs  This switch is on by default and cannot be turned off, thus it has no effect.  BUG=chromium:622501 BRANCH=none TEST=none  Change-Id: Ida50458504b501dbd7f630fd65111e920dc5a427 Signed-off-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362645 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="362645" owner_email="dnojiri@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/45/362645/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="If22e125a48f474b7f0dfeb162bc77bd603431ba1" commit="054c4975946220ae3e780eaf000ae728f9f19539" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ecryptfs: Have the kthread open the lower file under SELinux  When SELinux is enabled, files are associated with the current task's SID when they are opened. Before this change, the lower file would sometimes be associated with the SID of the first process to open the corresponding eCryptfs file. If a second process attempts to access this file through the same lower file, the access is denied unless the SELinux policy allows the second process to use files opened by the first process (the FD__USE permission).  Since it may not be desirable to allow all processes this permission, this change always opens the lower file from a thread with the kernel SID. This way, the policy only needs to grant all processes FD__USE on the kernel context (which in practice, is exactly the use of eCryptfs lower files).  Signed-off-by: Ricky Zhou &lt;rickyz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/337349 Reviewed-by: Gwendal G